.TH MINTCARE 1 "2026-10-13" "MintCare 1.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mintcare \- clean, optimise and repair Linux Mint
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mintcare
.RB [ \-\-tray ]
.br
.B mintcare
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without a command, MintCare opens its graphical window: diagnostics with one-click fixes,
reversible optimisations and profiles, a junk cleaner, disk-space and duplicate analysis,
Flatpak permissions, hardware health, boot analysis and scheduled check-ups.
Changes that need administrator rights ask for a password through polkit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR scan " [" \-\-fix ]
Run every check; with \-\-fix, apply the automatic fixes.
.TP
.BR tweaks " [" \-\-apply " ID...|recommended|profile:NAME | " \-\-revert " ID...]"
List, apply or revert optimisations. Profiles: desktop, gaming, laptop, developer.
.TP
.BR clean " [" \-\-run " [ID...]]"
Show what can be cleaned, or clean the default (or listed) items.
.TP
.B hardware
Drive SMART health, temperatures, throttling and boot time.
.TP
.BR space " [" PATH ]
Largest folders and files, and the number of Timeshift snapshots.
.TP
.BR report " [" \-o " FILE] [" \-\-personal ]
Write an HTML health report. Personal details are removed unless \-\-personal is given.
.TP
.BR maintain " [" \-\-no\-notify ]
The scheduled check-up: scan, safe user-level cleaning, desktop notification.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-tray
Start the window hidden in the system tray.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mintcare/settings.json
Settings.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/mintcare/history.jsonl
History of changes.
.TP
.I /var/lib/mintcare/
Records of applied optimisations, used to revert them.
